   "text": {
    "L1": "Body measures such as a handspan differ from person to person.",
    "L2": "So they can give different results. Standard units give the same result for everyone.",
    "L3": "A length has a number and a unit. The SI unit of length is the metre, or m.",
    "L4": "One metre is 100 centimetres, and one centimetre is 10 millimetres.",
    "L5": "Place the scale along the object, touching it, with one end at zero.",
    "L6": "If zero is broken, start at another full mark and subtract that starting mark.",
    "L7": "Here, 4.6 centimetres minus 1.0 centimetre gives 3.6 centimetres.",
    "L8": "Keep your eye directly above the end, not at an angle.",
    "L9": "Now choose the setup that gives a correct reading."
   },
